    "introduction": "David Lamelas is an Argentine artist. A pioneer of Conceptual Art, he was involved in Argentina's avant-garde scene in the 1960s. In 1968, he became the youngest Argentine ever to participate in the Venice Biennale with Office of Information about the Vietnam War at Three Levels: Visual Image, Text and Audio, an installation that shortly afterward was acquired by the Museum of Modern Art (MoMA) in New York. In 1993, he received a Guggenheim Fellowship for Fine Arts and in 1998, the DAAD Stipendium from Germany. Well known for his sculptures, performances and installations, Lamelas divides his time between Los Angeles, Buenos Aires, and Paris.",
